# Worktree & branch hygiene

Concurrent agents that branch-switch inside one checkout strand commits and drift `main`
(see the homeos incident in `~/Dev/_shared/lessons-learned/agent-worktree-hygiene.md`).
Make isolation the default:

- **One workstream = one branch = one worktree** under `.worktrees/` (gitignored). Use the
  `superpowers:using-git-worktrees` skill (or `git worktree add .worktrees/<name> -b <branch>`).
- Keep the **primary checkout on `main` and clean**. Don't switch branches there or accumulate
  unrelated uncommitted work.
- **Push feature branches early** — nothing should live only on local disk. Keep `main` in sync
  with what's deployed.
- An advisory `branch-guard` pre-commit hook warns when committing on `main`/`master` or a
  detached HEAD (`DEV_GUARD_STRICT=1` to enforce; `--no-verify` to override).
